WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.882
An idea.

2
00:00:01.042 --> 00:00:03.086
Every picture starts with an idea.

3
00:00:03.246 --> 00:00:05.846
It can come from a feeling, like being happy.

4
00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:07.957
From a place, like the market.

5
00:00:08.117 --> 00:00:10.300
From a story, a song, or the weather.

6
00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:12.224
You do not wait for an idea.

7
00:00:12.384 --> 00:00:14.010
You look around and find one.

8
00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:16.428
The material for the feeling.

9
00:00:16.588 --> 00:00:19.374
Once you have an idea, choose what to make it with.

10
00:00:19.534 --> 00:00:21.531
Bright paint for a happy picture.

11
00:00:21.691 --> 00:00:23.688
Soft pale chalk for a calm one.

12
00:00:23.848 --> 00:00:25.613
Dark charcoal for a storm.

13
00:00:25.773 --> 00:00:27.120
Glitter for a party.

14
00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:29.323
The material helps say what you mean.

15
00:00:30.023 --> 00:00:31.184
Adding something.

16
00:00:31.344 --> 00:00:33.945
Sometimes a picture does not say what you meant.

17
00:00:34.105 --> 00:00:35.498
The hair looks flat.

18
00:00:35.658 --> 00:00:37.283
You cannot tell it is windy.

19
00:00:37.443 --> 00:00:39.301
An artist does not start again.

20
00:00:39.461 --> 00:00:43.594
They add one thing: wool for the hair, bending trees for the wind.

21
00:00:44.294 --> 00:00:45.594
Trying something new.

22
00:00:45.754 --> 00:00:48.030
Artists try things they have never tried.

23
00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:49.583
Sand in the paint.

24
00:00:49.743 --> 00:00:50.997
Glue in the paint.

25
00:00:51.157 --> 00:00:53.432
Guess what it will do, try it, and look.

26
00:00:53.592 --> 00:00:57.122
Being brave with materials is how you find out what they can do.
